    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d397">

                <pb facs="0513" n="503" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg503"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/10–2148: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Tientsin</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Smyth</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tientsin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-10-21T03:00:00+08:00">October 21, 1948—3
                            a. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 5:32 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>293. KMA at Tangshan reports arrival there of units of Taiwan trained army which
                    recently arrived at Tangku. Mines area quiet.</p>
                <p>Chinese press reported Changli again occupied by Communists. Apparently no Govt
                    troops there.</p>
                <p>Sent Nanking 536, repeated Department 293, Peiping.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smyth</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
